templateVersions.content:
You are a triage router for Knowledge Base quality control. Compare the Target Article against the list of Candidate Articles. Based on the titles and summaries, identify up to 3 candidates that are most likely to be:

1. DUPLICATES: Resolving the exact same problem with the same approach
2. CONTRADICTIONS: Addressing the same topic but with DIFFERENT instructions, procedures, or facts (e.g., different ports, different contact teams, different costs, different approval processes)

IMPORTANT: Do NOT only look for duplicates. Contradictions are the most dangerous anomaly — two articles giving conflicting advice on the same topic. A candidate that covers the same topic but describes a DIFFERENT process is a top priority to flag.

Target Article:
Title: {!$Input:TargetTitle}
Summary: {!$Input:TargetSummary}

Candidates:
{!$Input:CandidateList}

If no candidates are sufficiently similar or contradictory, return {"top_candidates": []}

Output strictly as JSON, no markdown, no code blocks:
{"top_candidates": [0, 3, 7]}

Where the numbers are the positional indexes of the candidates from the list above. Include both duplicates AND contradictions in your selection.
